instrument wingie
; wingie-bird — the Wingie as it came, and then the caves under it
; fader1 Mix, fader2 Decay, fader3 Volume, as on the stock Wingie

2026-11-24 the bird
-------------------
; both keyboards play the resonator: strings on the left, a membrane on the right (keys2 is
; an octave up). The microphones ring them; every key also strikes its side.
the strings is wingie 2.18 string        ; 2.18 x 60 Hz: the C below middle C
the skin is wingie 2.18 membrane
the mixl is crossfade
the mixr is crossfade
the vol is quadvca

mic.left -> strings mixl.a
mic.right -> skin mixr.a
keys1.pitch -> strings.pitch
keys2.pitch -> skin.pitch
keys1.trig -> strings.strike
keys2.trig -> skin.strike
fader2 -> strings.decay skin.decay
strings -> mixl.b
skin -> mixr.b
fader1 -> mixl.mix mixr.mix
mixl -> vol.in1
mixr -> vol.in2
fader3 -> vol.cv1 vol.cv2
vol.out1 -> left
vol.out2 -> right
strings -> lights.left
skin -> lights.right

2026-11-24 the caves
--------------------
; the three factory caves: Low on the left, High on the right. The keys shift them by
; octaves and semitones; mode1 and mode2 strike them. fader1 Mix, fader2 Decay, fader3 Volume
the low is cave 1
the high is cave 3
the mix is crossfade
the vol is vca

mic.left -> low
mic.right -> high
keys1.pitch -> low.shift
keys2.pitch -> high.shift
mode1.tap -> low.strike
mode2.tap -> high.strike
fader2 -> low.decay high.decay
mic.both -> mix.a
low.odd high.even -> mix.b
fader1 -> mix.mix
fader3 -> vol.gain
mix -> vol -> out
low -> lights.left
high -> lights.right
